\par
\b Guide Questions and Answers\b0\par
\b 1. What state does the controller enter after reset?\b0\par
The controller enters S0 Main Green. Main road is green, side road is red, walk_light is off, and countdown is zero.\par
\par
\b 2. What is the required state order?\b0\par
The required order is S0 Main Green, S1 Main Yellow, S2 Side Green, S4 Walk if a pedestrian request is active, S3 Side Yellow, then back to S0 Main Green.\par
\par
\b 3. How does ped_request affect behavior?\b0\par
The ped_request signal creates a visible behavior change by adding the pedestrian walk state with countdown after the safe side-green phase.\par
\par
\b 4. How is safety guaranteed?\b0\par
Safety is guaranteed by preventing both roads from being green at the same time, using yellow transition states, activating walk only when both traffic lights are red, and returning to a safe state on reset.\par
\par
\b 5. What does the waveform prove?\b0\par
The waveform proves that the FSM follows the correct state order, changes timing in school mode, handles pedestrian requests safely, counts down during the walk state, supports flashing yellow mode, and resets safely.\par
